  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Arts &amp; Culture: Spotlights on Culture</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Spotlights on Culture is one of the Global Programmes through which the British Council delivers its grant-funded activity. The primary focus of this Global Programme is ODA eligible activity and outcomes.Spotlights on Culture is the UK&#x2019;s flagship international cultural programme, delivered with partners in priority countries and across the whole of the UK. The Spotlights on Culture programme leverages the diverse cultural assets of the whole of the UK to support greater international cultural collaboration and provide a high-profile platform in response to high-profile events or &#x2018;moments&#x2019; in the UK or in-country. What we do:There are two main areas of activity: 1. International Seasons and 2. UK Festivals.&#x25fc; 1. International Seasons with a focus on priority countries. Seasons are usually planned 2-3 years in advance.&#x25fc; 2. UK Festivals: Bespoke schemes that respond to needs / ambitions of one-off civic UK festival partners and their international objectives, for example UK Cities of Culture.Why we do it:&#x25fc; Increased opportunities for UK Arts, Culture and Creative sectors to foster international collaboration and showcasing&#x25fc; The cultural sector in the UK and globally understands its role in responding to global challenges of gender inequality and inclusion&#x25fc; Improved understanding and knowledge between people in range of contexts.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The audiences for this programme are:&#x25fc; Audiences. &#x25fc; Artists and art sector.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The programme energises and enables a wide range of stakeholders to participate and make new connections. The programme delivers ODA benefit through opportunities to collaborate and exchange and provides fantastic opportunities to showcase long-term work that drives positive social change, as well promote international tours and exhibitions by major UK institutions.The change we make:&#x25fc; 1. Audiences internationally have a greater engagement with, and favourability towards, UK Arts, culture and creativity.&#x25fc; 2. Increased access to safe spaces for dialogue and greater opportunities for plurality of expression.&#x25fc; 3. Learning and insights on current issues and trends are shared. &#x25fc; 4. Improve visibility, recognition and influence of women, disabled and other underrepresented creative professionals&#x25fc; 5. The UK&apos;s Arts, Culture and Creative sectors are better connected internationally, extending their profile and audiences.</narrative>
  </description>
